WEBVTT

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.930
You idiot! Where are you aiming at?!

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.800
Oh, dear. I've done it again.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.360
H-Hey! Are you just messing around?

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:26.710
First, you miss an easy fly ball,

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:29.530
then you have a strong arm,
but your control is non-existent!

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:31.920
Weren't you playing in the 
American little leagues?!

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:36.180
Huh? This is the first time 
I've ever played baseball.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:38.260
<i>What?!</i>

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:14.820
Y-Your first time playing baseball?!

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:18.070
The Two Juniors

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:22.450
Yes. I play baseball for the first time.

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:24.000
Okay?

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:25.850
I don't believe you!

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:28.160
You're Satou Toshiya's son.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:33.780
There's no way that's true!

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:34.800
Hey, you over there!

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:37.350
Get back to your positions!

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:38.130
Y-Yes, sorry!

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:42.340
We're in the middle of a game, for Pete's sake.

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:46.170
That error came at a bad time.

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:50.770
Yeah. Satou's mistake has cost us three runs.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:50.770
Team

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:50.770
Guts

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:50.770
Dolphins

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:54.480
Do you think it's possible 
he's terrible at baseball?

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:55.360
It's possible.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:58.240
He's got quite an arm, though.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:04.090
There aren't many sixth graders who can 
throw a ball from outfield to the bench.

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:07.290
Guess he's inherited his father's good arm.

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:09.790
The same can't be said for Daigo.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:11.740
I told you to not say things like that.

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:12.880
Sorry, sorry.

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:14.670
Strike! Batter out!

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:18.470
<i>Could this really be his 
first time playing baseball?</i>

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:22.340
<i>Sure, he made a complete hash of
what should've been a basic play.</i>

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:26.170
<i>That throw back, though...</i>

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:30.140
<i>He's certainly got more 
natural talent than I do.</i>

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:31.200
Right field!

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:33.020
Got it!

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:35.440
Out!

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:38.170
Nice catch.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:42.360
What?!

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:44.570
This is your first time playing baseball?!

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:45.740
Yes.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:50.830
In America, I played soccer, 
basketball, and tennis.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.990
I played whatever sport was in-season,

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:56.590
but the nearest I got to baseball 
was playing catch with my dad.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:57.820
Are you serious?!

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:02.590
He said I could take up baseball whenever,
so I should try other sports while young.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:05.830
That's what they do over there, anyway.

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:12.040
But in Japan, you have a custom of picking
one sports team in middle school, right?

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:16.110
That's why I decided to take this 
opportunity to give baseball a try.

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:18.340
Give it... a try?

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:19.560
I see.

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:21.340
That explains all those errors.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:25.400
Our bad for assuming you were experienced
just because you're Satou's son.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:26.380
Don't worry about it.

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:29.200
All right, who's up to bat?

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:32.960
The previous inning ended with Daigo,
so that means it's...

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:34.390
Satou's next, sir.

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:36.300
He subbed in for me, the leadoff.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:37.460
Huh? Me?

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:40.170
Yes. It's your first ever at bat.

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:41.630
All right!

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:42.670
Time to do some batting!

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:44.530
Hey! Your helmet!

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:46.590
Thank you.

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:47.810
Play ball!

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:00.240
Strike!

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:03.160
What kind of swing was that?

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:04.240
Hey, don't laugh.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:06.070
He's never played before. He can't help it.

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:07.170
Huh?

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:12.900
Strike two!

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:17.520
He's never gonna hit it like that.

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:19.640
Time out!

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:21.960
Hey, Satou.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:24.010
Let me take a look at your grip.

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:26.610
I knew it. That's the wrong way around.

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:28.650
That's a left-hander's grip.

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:29.970
"Wrong way around"?

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:33.330
A right-handed batter holds it like this.

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:34.100
Like this.

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:35.750
Uh-huh.

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:39.900
I see.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:42.160
No wonder it seemed 
hard to swing it like that.

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:43.060
Play ball!

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:45.340
<i>Seriously?</i>

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:48.020
<i>The Dolphins have a complete 
novice on their team.</i>

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:58.120
No way! He got a hit
off his first proper swing!

00:05:59.350 --> 00:06:00.900
Yes! I hit it! I hit it!

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:03.010
Hey! Run to first!

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:05.400
Out!

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:09.000
Isn't it weird to be called out
when I got a hit?

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:10.680
The only thing that's weird here is <i>you!</i>

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:12.630
<i>D-Damn him.</i>

00:06:12.630 --> 00:06:14.140
<i>He ended up getting out,</i>

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:18.190
<i>but he got a hit like it was nothing!
I've only ever done that in my dreams!</i>

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:21.890
<i>He middled it as soon as
I showed him how to hold the bat?</i>

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:25.440
<i>Is this what a real second coming is like?</i>

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:28.350
Final inning.

00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:30.780
One out, runners on first and third.

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:32.960
Things are looking bleak.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:38.160
Daigo!

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:41.250
No! I'm not going to make it.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:53.300
To first! The runner jumped the gun!

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:56.390
And he's out!

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:58.060
Yes!

00:06:58.060 --> 00:06:59.440
A double play!

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:03.730
Yup, I'm getting the hang of it now.

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:07.150
Baseball's surprisingly easy,
 isn't it, Daigo-kun?

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:13.830
<i>Daigo's team now has
one last chance on offense.</i>

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:15.360
<i>I have to watch the finale up close.</i>

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:19.040
<i>That kid in center field 
has an incredible throw.</i>

00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:21.540
<i>He looked like a total novice at first...</i>

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:29.080
<i>That man...</i>

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:30.840
<i>Could it be...</i>

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:38.320
It <i>is</i> Toshi-kun!

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:39.690
But what's he doing here?

00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:40.460
Toshi-kun!

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:41.930
Watch out!

00:07:41.930 --> 00:07:42.480
Huh?

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:52.820
Out!

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:55.620
So unlucky.

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:58.640
Final inning. Two outs. 
Only one more chance.

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:00.330
Looks like we're gonna lose this one.

00:08:01.700 --> 00:08:03.180
<i>It's finally over.</i>

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:05.870
<i>I'm only here to make up the numbers,</i>

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:08.350
<i>so I guess I won't have to
play baseball anymore.</i>

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:14.720
<i>We're both "seconds", but there's
 such a wide gap between us.</i>

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:17.720
<i>In his first at bat,  he got
a hit like it was child's play.</i>

00:08:18.070 --> 00:08:20.220
<i>He can already track fly balls.</i>

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:22.290
<i>And he has a monster of an arm.</i>

00:08:23.450 --> 00:08:24.700
<i>He's what I wanted to be.</i>

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:28.950
<i>He's the kind of "second" I wanted to be.</i>

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:32.400
So you're not taking up baseball again?

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:37.400
We're both "seconds", and we're in 
the same year at the same school.

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:40.620
Personally, I'd get a kick out 
of playing here with you.

00:08:41.110 --> 00:08:43.660
But baseball doesn't make you happy, does it?

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:47.940
No, I'm not happy.

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:51.630
If I was a talented "second" 
like you, I'd probably be happy.

00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:53.240
I wonder about that...

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:56.510
Having talent and enjoying a 
sport are two different things.

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:04.390
Truth is, I gave baseball a try today,
but I don't find it particularly fun yet.

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:05.770
What?!

00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:11.070
Safe!

00:09:11.510 --> 00:09:12.480
Lucky!

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:13.860
We got a runner on base!

00:09:14.060 --> 00:09:17.740
Do you think everyone here has 
the talents you're talking about?

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:21.890
Even if they don't, they look happy to me.

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:24.420
All right! It's not over yet!

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:25.790
Keep it going, Matsuda!

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:28.670
Yeah, but they're not "seconds."

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:32.380
There isn't hype about them 
every time they play baseball.

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:35.240
Nobody's comparing them to their fathers,

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:38.800
and they won't get an inferiority 
complex over their lack of talent!

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:42.640
Ball.

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:44.840
Oh, I get it now.

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:47.890
You never really cared 
about playing baseball...

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:52.460
You just wanted baseball to make you 
famous, like it did your father.

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:56.400
Of course your lack of talent 
would make you want to quit.

00:09:57.420 --> 00:09:58.670
Hey, Daigo!

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:00.860
You're up next.

00:10:00.860 --> 00:10:02.160
Hurry up and get ready.

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:03.040
O-Okay.

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:10.030
Dead ball!

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:15.090
Yeah, but Daigo's up next.

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:17.200
It's over. We've got
the awful junior at the plate!

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:18.140
Hey!

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:20.320
What's wrong with you guys?!

00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:22.510
Can't you cheer him on
 like any other guy?

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:26.080
It's because of teammates like you 
that Daigo quit in the first place!

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:28.320
Hit it, Daigo!

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:29.440
I know you hate it!

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:32.290
The least you can do is get one last hit

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:34.820
and silence me, those guys,
and everyone else!

00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:47.250
Play ball!

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:51.340
Ball.

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:55.830
You never really cared 
about playing baseball...

00:10:56.170 --> 00:11:00.170
You just wanted baseball to make you 
famous, like it did your father.

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:03.940
<i>Where does he get off, 
mouthing off like that?</i>

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:06.680
<i>It's not about being famous.</i>

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:09.220
<i>This is something I really wanted!</i>

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:13.730
<i>I really wanted to be a 
cool player, just like Pop!</i>

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:17.900
<i>I couldn't enjoy it despite having no talent!</i>

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:22.160
<i>My love for baseball wasn't that shallow!</i>

00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:27.410
Daigo, run!

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:32.250
Damn it! Damn it! Damn it!

00:11:40.030 --> 00:11:41.080
Safe!

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:42.310
Alright!

00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:43.680
Daigo kept the inning alive!

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:44.680
Bases loaded!

00:11:44.840 --> 00:11:45.740
Yes!

00:11:45.740 --> 00:11:47.680
There it is! His first hit!

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:51.590
No...

00:11:51.590 --> 00:11:55.470
I don't want this graze that barely
qualifies as a hit to be my first hit.

00:12:01.830 --> 00:12:04.840
<i>That was a seriously questionable 
and awkward first hit,</i>

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:07.070
<i>but everyone seems really happy about it.</i>

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:11.080
We're counting on you, Satou!

00:12:13.200 --> 00:12:14.390
I've got this.

00:12:15.350 --> 00:12:19.670
I cost the team three runs with my glove,
so I need to get them all back with my bat.

00:12:23.570 --> 00:12:24.460
Play ball!

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:35.900
Strike.

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:39.740
Hey, that was way high!

00:12:39.740 --> 00:12:41.570
Why did you swing at it?

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:49.520
<i>Is it possible that he's not even trying 
to judge if it'll be a ball or a strike?</i>

00:12:50.110 --> 00:12:52.730
<i>I mean, he didn't even 
know how to hold a bat.</i>

00:12:52.730 --> 00:12:54.290
<i>So it's totally possible.</i>

00:12:55.610 --> 00:12:56.790
<i>Don't throw strikes.</i>

00:12:57.440 --> 00:12:58.720
<i>Keep it outside.</i>

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:04.860
Strike two.

00:13:05.940 --> 00:13:07.720
What is he doing?!

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:09.760
He doesn't know what the strike zone is.

00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:11.520
<i>I knew it.</i>

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:12.770
<i>I called it correctly.</i>

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:14.110
Time out!

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:17.230
<i>Hey, now. This can't be happening...</i>

00:13:18.700 --> 00:13:20.880
<i>Yup, he's explaining zones.</i>

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:26.180
<i>He really doesn't know anything about
baseball despite being a pro's son.</i>

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:29.910
And?

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:31.760
Just as we thought. He didn't know.

00:13:32.420 --> 00:13:35.390
Anyway, I've explained zones to him now.

00:13:36.760 --> 00:13:39.410
<i>I see. So if you ignore the balls</i>

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:42.630
<i>and only swing at strikes, 
you've got a better chance of getting a hit.</i>

00:13:43.370 --> 00:13:44.820
<i>Where was it again?</i>

00:13:45.310 --> 00:13:49.440
<i>The height is between chest and knees,
 and the width is the width of the plate.</i>

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:53.190
<i>Pitches in this area are strikes.</i>

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:54.330
Play ball!

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:57.300
<i>Does he know about the strike zone now?</i>

00:13:57.640 --> 00:14:00.950
<i>Whatever. If I pitch to the corners,
he's bound to swing.</i>

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:05.310
Ball!

00:14:06.170 --> 00:14:07.780
<i>His first take, huh?</i>

00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:10.620
<i>Nah, he just couldn't swing.</i>

00:14:14.310 --> 00:14:15.170
Ball!

00:14:16.270 --> 00:14:17.370
<i>This guy...</i>

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:20.880
<i>Does he really know where his 
strike zone is to the last inch now?</i>

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:22.540
<i>What's with this guy?</i>

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:25.410
<i>That one was close to being a strike, 
and he didn't move a muscle.</i>

00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:27.880
<i>It's a 2-2 count.</i>

00:14:28.350 --> 00:14:29.380
<i>Bases loaded.</i>

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:31.580
<i>We can't afford to fall behind in the count.</i>

00:14:32.410 --> 00:14:35.100
<i>Oh, well. We've gotta go
right at him with a strike!</i>

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:47.550
That's gone long!

00:14:47.550 --> 00:14:48.280
Move it!

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:51.700
<i>What the hell was that hit?</i>

00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:55.200
First run.

00:14:56.060 --> 00:14:57.500
Now, we're even!

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:00.670
Go for home, Daigo!

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:04.460
<i>That rookie isn't normal!</i>

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:06.230
All right! We're gonna win!

00:15:06.230 --> 00:15:07.170
Go!

00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:09.170
Daigo!

00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:12.140
<i>If I make it to home, we win.</i>

00:15:29.140 --> 00:15:30.150
Out!

00:15:32.580 --> 00:15:34.200
And that's game!

00:15:41.030 --> 00:15:43.980
So it was a tie. Big deal.

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:49.050
The manager took the blame 
for letting you play in sneakers.

00:15:53.730 --> 00:15:56.740
B-Besides, you really gave it 
everything you had out there!

00:15:56.740 --> 00:15:59.920
You got your first hit, and you 
made a number of good plays!

00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:03.560
It's been a while since I've 
gotten so into a game like that.

00:16:03.720 --> 00:16:06.040
It made me appreciate 
baseball all over again!

00:16:07.220 --> 00:16:08.440
Don't you see, Daigo?

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:11.880
You've gotta take what you're feeling now
and pour it back into your baseba—

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:12.320
Not gonna happen.

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:18.570
If you were trying to make me consider
playing again by putting me in that game.

00:16:20.300 --> 00:16:22.600
Well, it looks like your 
plan completely backfired!

00:16:22.600 --> 00:16:27.090
Satou Toshiya's son helped me
 give up on baseball once and for all!

00:16:32.770 --> 00:16:35.680
Hey! What the hell?!

00:16:36.050 --> 00:16:40.060
You said if I played in that game,
you'd buy me a new console!

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:43.960
I told you already. I'll only buy it 
if you take up baseball again.

00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:45.980
You can't just spend all day playing games.

00:16:46.290 --> 00:16:48.690
Jeez, they're so loud.

00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:50.260
That's so unfair!

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:53.700
You deceived me just 
so I'd play in that game!

00:16:54.820 --> 00:16:57.600
Yes, I did. If I hadn't said that, 
you wouldn't have gone!

00:16:57.600 --> 00:17:00.670
Besides, you've also been deceiving us.

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:02.700
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.670
Izumi told me all about it.

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:08.580
How you've been pretending to study hard so 
you can take the Fuurin Academy entrance,

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:10.710
but in reality, you have no 
intention of going there.

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:16.760
What are you guys fighting about
this early in the morning?

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:18.970
Shut up, you gossiping old hag!

00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:20.000
What?

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:23.100
All right, fine! Whatever! You liar!

00:17:28.220 --> 00:17:29.740
Did something happen?

00:17:31.340 --> 00:17:35.610
Ah, okay. So Satou Toshiya's son 
was at yesterday's game.

00:17:35.980 --> 00:17:36.940
Yes.

00:17:36.940 --> 00:17:40.340
And despite being a complete novice, 
he displayed some impressive skills.

00:17:40.340 --> 00:17:42.260
Which people might 
attribute to his lineage.

00:17:42.260 --> 00:17:45.620
So Birdbrain compared himself to this guy 
and got upset about it?

00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:47.210
What an idiot.

00:17:48.340 --> 00:17:52.780
But at this rate, he might 
really quit baseball.

00:17:53.090 --> 00:17:54.660
What the hell, man?!

00:17:54.660 --> 00:17:56.800
She totally went back on her word!

00:17:57.260 --> 00:17:59.580
A promise is a promise!

00:18:02.300 --> 00:18:05.140
And then came epic face plant...

00:18:05.140 --> 00:18:06.600
That's hilarious!

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:12.010
And then came the epic face plant...

00:18:16.150 --> 00:18:17.900
Good morning, Daigo-kun.

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:19.860
You guys...

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:24.500
Oh, we happen to live near each other,
 so we walk the same route to school.

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:25.080
Right?

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:26.120
Y-Yeah.

00:18:26.280 --> 00:18:28.450
Who cares about that?

00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:33.840
I'm sorry for my "epic face plant"!

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:38.340
I'm glad you guys find it so funny that 
I'm a complete failure as a "second"!

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:40.760
You guys are just horrible!

00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:44.780
Daigo-kun?

00:18:45.380 --> 00:18:46.570
What was that about?

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:50.150
<i>This is the worst.</i>

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:52.650
<i>I can't put my trust in anything anymore.</i>

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:56.200
<i>Thanks to baseball, 
I can't even see my future.</i>

00:18:58.270 --> 00:19:02.400
<i>Ah, man, I want to play the rest of my game.</i>

00:19:04.820 --> 00:19:07.160
I'll buy it for you if you play baseball.

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:08.750
<i>No, no, no!</i>

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:11.170
<i>I can't possibly play baseball just for that!</i>

00:19:11.740 --> 00:19:16.460
<i>Thanks to </i>that<i> guy, my standing 
is even worse than before!</i>

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:20.810
<i>I never, ever want to play 
baseball with that guy again!</i>

00:19:22.970 --> 00:19:24.630
What's the matter, Shigeno-kun?

00:19:24.630 --> 00:19:26.470
Ah, it's nothing.

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:27.880
Go to the nurse if you're ill.

00:19:27.880 --> 00:19:29.480
I'm fine, really!

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:33.740
Shigeno-kun?

00:19:48.340 --> 00:19:49.620
Hey!

00:19:52.070 --> 00:19:55.800
I-It's not like I really want 
to talk to you, either.

00:19:56.460 --> 00:19:59.090
But Satou-kun asked me to.

00:20:01.600 --> 00:20:05.410
He was telling me about how he fell 
during sports day one time at his old school.

00:20:05.410 --> 00:20:09.350
He thinks you might have misinterpreted it
and thought he was talking about you.

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:13.900
Don't be a jerk.

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:18.450
I might hate you, but I don't make 
fun of people behind their backs.

00:20:19.700 --> 00:20:20.870
Really?

00:20:22.250 --> 00:20:26.030
Oh, yeah, another thing 
on the baseball front...

00:20:26.250 --> 00:20:28.960
Satou-kun said he won't 
be joining the Dolphins.

00:20:29.450 --> 00:20:32.290
He asked me to tell you 
he won't be taking up baseball.

00:20:32.520 --> 00:20:33.430
What?!

00:20:36.950 --> 00:20:39.840
I'll take out the trash, so you guys can go.

00:20:39.840 --> 00:20:41.280
Thanks, Satou-kun!

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:42.120
See you!

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:43.350
Bye!

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:45.970
Satou-kun's nice, isn't he?

00:20:52.400 --> 00:20:53.800
Daigo-kun?

00:20:54.930 --> 00:20:56.100
What's up?

00:20:56.100 --> 00:20:58.190
If it's about this morning, 
I already told Sakura-sa—

00:20:58.190 --> 00:21:01.010
Yeah, she told me. Water under the bridge.

00:21:01.420 --> 00:21:04.200
More importantly, are you serious 
about not playing baseball?!

00:21:07.060 --> 00:21:09.050
Deadly serious.

00:21:09.050 --> 00:21:11.560
I tried baseball for the 
first time yesterday,

00:21:11.990 --> 00:21:15.460
and it really did nothing for me.

00:21:16.160 --> 00:21:17.950
I mean, it's just boring.

00:21:17.950 --> 00:21:20.450
On defense, the ball rarely comes to you,

00:21:20.450 --> 00:21:23.590
and on offense, you've gotta wait 
for like eight other guys to bat.

00:21:24.690 --> 00:21:26.470
What are you talking about?

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:28.710
You have so much talent! What's your issue?!

00:21:28.710 --> 00:21:30.760
It'd clearly be a total waste!

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:32.640
A waste?

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:35.770
What are <i>you</i> talking about? 
Are you some kind of scout now?

00:21:37.040 --> 00:21:38.040
Shut up!

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:41.770
I'm telling you to stop screwing around!

00:21:44.180 --> 00:21:46.620
You can hit well, throw well,
 and defend well.

00:21:47.440 --> 00:21:51.420
You have every single thing that
I'd give anything to have myself.

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:54.590
You can make all those cool plays...

00:21:56.110 --> 00:21:57.710
So don't you dare say that it's boring!

00:22:01.110 --> 00:22:02.000
Don't you dare...

00:22:03.630 --> 00:22:06.420
Daigo-kun, you really like baseball, don't you?

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:10.900
For my part, I really don't 
understand why you quit.

00:22:10.900 --> 00:22:13.460
I mean, you really love baseball, don't you?

00:22:16.010 --> 00:22:19.810
Okay, let's play baseball together.

00:22:19.810 --> 00:22:22.000
If you return to the Dolphins,

00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:25.190
I'll try to figure out the appeal of 
baseball by playing some more.

00:22:25.690 --> 00:22:27.120
What?!

00:22:27.120 --> 00:22:30.030
Where did that come from?!

00:24:00.990 --> 00:24:01.710
Why?

00:24:02.340 --> 00:24:03.870
Why do I, the talentless wonder,

00:24:03.870 --> 00:24:07.340
have to tag along with 
Mr. Talented to play baseball?!

00:24:07.720 --> 00:24:12.510
And we're already being pitted against
the Dolphins' starting battery.

00:24:12.510 --> 00:24:14.010
This is moving way too fast.

00:24:14.340 --> 00:24:15.760
Can I even survive this?

00:24:16.790 --> 00:24:19.500
Next time: "The Talent of Loving Baseball".

00:24:18.010 --> 00:24:25.020
The Talent of Loving Baseball

00:24:19.900 --> 00:24:21.800
Run to the stage of your dreams!
